imes but I didn't want this cause it  would be quite visible and that's why  placing it on this side of this hill  felt like a good way to sort of get that  in and what will hopefully help with  that is going to be the rock work and  sweet Jesus it's gonna be a lot of rock  work it's basically going to fill this  entire side of the hill and it did feel  like a pretty big risk like at the time  I just sort of jumped into it like Yolo  I'm just gonna place rocks all over the  side of this hill and see how it turns  out for the park but there was a bit of  an idea behind it I thought it would be  cool to have some rock work instead of  the the terrain in the game itself since  you know you can't really got any steep  slopes but even though while this isn't  really too steep of a slope I wanted to  have a really steep cliff face right  underneath the lifts able to show to  give you a wall as a background sort of  backdrop to have the coaster run against  yeah you can't really do that with a  train since it's well not very steep and  especially this Hill is almost like a  roller coaster tycoon one hero it's just  a very square ish here with some steps  it's almost like you can have some rice  plantations on the side of it and yeah I  didn't really want to have that sort of  hero I wanted it to be quite rocky quite  steep more like a cliff face than gentle  grassy hill and the only real option to  do that seemed to be to just have a lot  of rock work on top of it so this is  like that really massive rock work to  Sanders sort of sculpt a mountain here  instead of just the smaller details  though at this point I'm getting into  the details as well adding some small  rocks all around this just to you know  make it look a bit more interesting than  just one big collection of huge rocks  until you get some smaller boulders in  down there and they also help to kind of  connect it to the rest of the area I  always like to when I do my rock work  have some smaller books that sort of  scatter around the larger rocks  especially on the bottom of it kind of  like the pebbles that break out of rocks  in real life and that you see kind of  collecting in these streams of sand and  small rocks that you see underneath real  rock facades  and it just all connects it a little bit  more to the sand because having large  rocks and to the sand it kind of  connected more to the grass area around  it because having like really big rocks  right next to grass with no way of a  real transition just very often seems  very like abrupt and very sudden and  like it doesn't really fit together and  glide into each other very smoothly and  I think the small rocks can help quite a  bit with that as well I also like to do  it in this order because you know it's  it's a lot easier if you kind of start  off with sculpting out the general shape  of the rock work that you want to make  with very large rocks first and then get  into the detailing and you know making  the rocks look nice on the outside by  using the smaller rocks to get that bit  of texturing in  most of the time is definitely gonna  stick in making the small rocks and  adding those all around it and it's  quite a bit of a tedious process as well  especially if you're way too  perfectionist and picky like I am  sometimes it like you can sing quite a  bit of time into placing these very  small rocks all around the sides and  having like the the placements of them  just rights but I was quite happy with  how it looks at this point now it did  look like one very big gray blob which  doesn't really mix well into the rest of  the area at this point so adding some  trees to it I thought would help to make  this London a little bit nicer with the  park and make this a little bit less  like one big great barren wasteland of  rock and the trees are falling over  because of heavy gravity of pulse mode  at the moment which does make it a  little harder to they'll get an idea of  what it looks like though I still like  to play on pulse mode I'm not really  sure where that really comes from it's a  bit of a habit actually from other games  which do have a day and night mode at  least vanilla and that's you know you  sort of want to have a certain time of  day but I guess over here I didn't  really want the rain to appear and it  appeared like a little bit ago and I  didn't want to really have to do with  that again is you know you can see  things a little bit more clearly when  it's not raining so I put up with the  very strange-looking trees for well a  couple of times just before going back  to real time for a little bit and have  them actually you know go back into the  position that they should be I do hope  this bug which I also think appeared  quite recently gets fixed at some point  in the future because it is quite  strange even though it can be really  funny as well now I'm obviously talking  about that because this is pretty much  just three placements and it's not that  interesting just kind of standard trees  throwing in a couple of those red  poplars or yeah they're poplars a couple  of those red poplars to get a bit more  of a Japanese vibe to it I thought it  would be nicer to you know get some red  regular trees in maybe some other kind  of colors but it's pretty hard to fit  those in when it comes to you know the  space since they are  large and the poplars are just so easy  to get into all sorts of small spaces  and especially around the rock work here  I didn't want any trees that are half  drowning in the rock work so it was  quite tough to get them into the exact  spaces and I did want to have like most  of the trees just be green pine trees to  get a pine tree forest and look through  this part of the park much like the rest  of the park just to have that fit into  the climate in which this is supposed to  be and even though I have no idea what  the exact climate of this point would be  or where Cydonia Hills us even located  like what kind of country will even call  a theme park Cydonia hills it doesn't  really make any sense  by the way yes I did name it after  Knights of Cydonia it but that's a story  for another time actually because this  time-lapse is ending so maybe we'll have  story time with silver at some time  later but thank you guys for watching  this video and I hope to see you guys  next time
 

